# A335585

The numbers visited on a square spiral, with a(n) = n for 1 <= n <= 3, when stepping to an unvisited number as close as possible to the n = 1 starting position that has at least one common factor with the second last visited number but none with the last visited number. In case of a tie, choose the smallest number.

The 74 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

